From b1f608189c0526391f2457e4ac01d7c0a2ce2b58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:51:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: read worker-created cards from the board
 replica; refuse their writes as foreign_card naming the owner; show
 ready-card queue position

A card created on a Board worker node (worker-1) is in no Desktop-reachable gateway's live kanban.db: a synced
board's live file holds only that gateway's own cards, the replica (kanban/sync-shadow/<board>.db) holds the whole
board. GET /api/plugins/kanban/tasks/{id} read only the live file, so cross_task read answered "not found on any
connected gateway" and a chat concluded the card was a phantom (t_01a19fd40c53bb19). Writes answered stale_run /
"cannot archive" / "unknown id or terminal state".

- hermes_cli/kanban_foreign_card.py: replica path for a synced board (kanban.sync.enabled + boards), read-only open
  (mode=ro, query_only fallback), owner_of/refusal/check, rejection "foreign_card".
- GET /tasks/{id}: live hit adds "source": "live" (+ "queue" when ready); a live miss on a synced board reads the
  replica and adds "source": "replica", "owner": <created_on>; a miss in both stays 404.
- 409 "foreign_card: <id> was created on <owner> and lives there; ..." on POST /tasks/{id}/comments and PATCH
  /tasks/{id}; kanban_complete (new rejection class foreign_card), kanban_archive and kanban_comment tool paths; CLI
  `hermes kanban complete` / `archive`. A pickup copy in the live file is unchanged (completes into the outbox).
- hermes_cli/kanban_queue_position.py: ready live cards get queue {lane: local, ahead, running, limit,
  approximate} (ahead = same-assignee unclaimed, non-worker-first ready cards with higher priority or same priority
  and older), or
  {lane: worker_pool, reason: <kanban_queue_reason code>} for worker-first-v1 cards. Other statuses: no key.

Proof: tests/plugins/test_kanban_foreign_card_api.py (16) + tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_foreign_card_writes.py
(9, incl. two-gateway fake-Board e2e). Parent: 12 fail (404 / KeyError source,queue / stale_run / generic
messages); the 8 controls (missing-everywhere 404, unsynced board 404, live comment, done card no queue, unknown id
stale_run, pickup copy completes) pass on both. Fix: 25/25 (3 later guard tests: no-replica 404 creates no file, replica_path of the replica itself, created_on without the sync column). Mutants killed: dropping claim_lock IS NULL from ahead, dropping the live-file check in owner_of (pickup e2e fails). Regression: tests/plugins + complete/archive tool
suites + test_kanban_cli + test_kanban_worker_node, 2090 passed. Live probe on hermes-hub's real board:
t_01a1a36257482229 (created_on=worker-1) -> 200 source=replica owner=worker-1; a ready hub card ->
queue {lane: local, ahead: 2, running: 9, limit: 7}.

Card: t_01a1a015ef0013bd

Desktop half (prefers a live holder over a replica answer, passes foreign_card verbatim): hermes-mods e18a3768.
Review (Opus): its blocking finding (a replica answer shadowing a reachable live holder in cross_task) is fixed
there; probe-failure connection leak fixed + tested; worker-first cards excluded from the local `ahead`.
Out of scope, unchanged (still the old generic errors on replica-only cards): attachments, delete, reclaim,
specify, reassign, block/unblock, move, link, CLI comment/block/edit/assign, kanban_show.
